{#-
  Fallback chat template for models whose tokenizer defines none (common for
  base/completion-only checkpoints such as allenai/OLMo-2-0425-1B -- as of
  transformers v4.44, vLLM's OpenAI-compatible /v1/chat/completions endpoint
  hard-errors instead of falling back to an implicit default in that case).
  Only used by start-template.sh when the model directory has no
  chat_template of its own and the workflow's `model.chat_template` input is
  left blank -- see that script for the detection logic.

  Renders the "### Instruction:\n<user>\n\n### Response:\n<assistant>"
  (Alpaca) layout, the convention such checkpoints are instruction-tuned
  against, so a fine-tuned base model is served in the format it was trained
  on. Multi-turn history renders as repeated pairs of the same two headers.
-#}
{%- if messages[0]['role'] == 'system' -%}
{{ messages[0]['content'] }}{{ "\n\n" }}
{%- set messages = messages[1:] -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- for message in messages -%}
{%- if message['role'] == 'user' -%}
### Instruction:
{{ message['content'] }}

{% elif message['role'] == 'assistant' -%}
### Response:
{{ message['content'] }}

{% endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if add_generation_prompt -%}
### Response:
{% endif -%}
